=ICP description: {{ $('Configure me').first().json.icp_description }}

Overlap changes on the user's own accounts this week (JSON). change is one of: now_shared_with_partners (an existing account of the user that newly appears in partners' data), new_partner (another partner now has it), partner_opportunity (a partner opened a deal on it). new_partners shows at most 8 names, new_partner_count is the full count:
{{ JSON.stringify($json.overlap_changes.map(x => ({ record_id: x.record_id, account: x.record_name, website: x.website, change: x.change === 'new_account' ? 'now_shared_with_partners' : x.change, new_partners: (x.new_partners || []).slice(0, 8), new_partner_count: (x.new_partners || []).length, partner_count: x.partner_count, a_partner_has_open_opportunity: x.has_partner_opp }))) }}

Net-new accounts (JSON):
{{ JSON.stringify($json.net_new_accounts.map(x => ({ domain: x.domain, name: x.account_name, industry: x.industry, country: x.country, employee_range: x.employee_range, customer_of_partners: x.partner_list, coverage_score: x.coverage_score }))) }}

Suggested partners (JSON):
{{ JSON.stringify($json.partner_suggestions.map(x => ({ domain: x.domain, name: x.partner_name }))) }}

Return the brief JSON. In why and next_step, write for the rep: state facts, never describe what the tools did or did not return.

